{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Who silences</b> — like תשבחם משקים, in the manner of: <i>you rule the pride of the sea</i>, because he mentioned <i>and the distant seas</i>." "And the meaning of <i>and the tumult of nations</i> — those likened to water, like: <i>the mighty waters of the river</i>. And so HaShem will deliver them from drought and from distress."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {0 "Resolved reading of תשבחם משקיע/משקים uncertain; rendered as quoted Hebrew form."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:44.654826595Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}